ثلاثة أبعاد: $u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$.","En":"Three-dimensional dot product: $u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"حواصل ضرب المركبات المناظرة 4 و0 و−5.","En":"Corresponding component products are 4, 0 and −5."},{"Ar":"نجمعها: 4+0−5=−1.","En":"Sum them: 4+0−5=−1."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$-1$","En":"$-1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تحوّل −1 في المتجه إلى +1.","En":"Do not turn the vector's −1 into +1."},"FormulaLatex":"u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3","Substitution":{"Ar":"$4+0-5$","En":"$4+0-5$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"المركبة الثانية تسهم بصفر، و4−5=−1.","En":"The second contributes zero, and 4−5=−1."}},"TrackIds":[14,20],"CategoryId":14,"PrimarySkillId":63,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"لا تجمع المركبات قبل ضربها.","En":"Do not add the components before multiplying."},{"Ar":"احسب ثلاثة نواتج ضرب للمركبات المناظرة ثم اجمعها.","En":"Compute three corresponding component products, then sum them."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون الضرب النقطي في ثلاثة أبعاد: $u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$.","En":"Three-dimensional dot product: $u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"حواصل ضرب المركبات المناظرة 4 و0 و−5.","En":"Corresponding component products are 4, 0 and −5."},{"Ar":"نجمعها: 4+0−5=−1.","En":"Sum them: 4+0−5=−1."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$-1$","En":"$-1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تحوّل −1 في المتجه إلى +1.","En":"Do not turn the vector's −1 into +1."},"FormulaLatex":"u\\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3","Substitution":{"Ar":"$4+0-5$","En":"$4+0-5$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"المركبة الثانية تسهم بصفر، و4−5=−1.","En":"The second contributes zero, and 4−5=−1."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"−9 يجعل حاصل ضرب المركبة الأولى سالباً.","En":"−9 incorrectly makes the first product negative."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 يعكس إشارة 4−5.","En":"1 reverses the sign of 4−5."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"9 يتجاهل الإشارة السالبة للمركبة الثالثة.","En":"9 ignores the negative third component."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$قانون الضرب النقطي في ثلاثة أبعاد: $u\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$.

$u\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$

1. حواصل ضرب المركبات المناظرة 4 و0 و−5.

2. نجمعها: 4+0−5=−1.

$4+0-5$

$-1$ بلا وحدة قياس

المركبة الثانية تسهم بصفر، و4−5=−1.

لا تحوّل −1 في المتجه إلى +1.$mw$,$mw$Three-dimensional dot product: $u\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$.

$u\cdot v=u_1v_1+u_2v_2+u_3v_3$

1. Corresponding component products are 4, 0 and −5.

2. Sum them: 4+0−5=−1.

$4+0-5$

$-1$ Dimensionless

The second contributes zero, and 4−5=−1.

Do not turn the vector's −1 into +1.$mw$),
(695,647,$mw$F0AAA7F460D6B903D2C5D05A8245E67CC2E741C1D521D5FCFDC5995D79F04F09$mw$,$mw$d53e2a37d0280fbad1d8f409af50e3ff$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":647,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":14,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"استنتاج مركبة مجهولة من شرط التعامد","TitleEn":"Find an unknown vector component from orthogonality","QuestionTextAr":"المتجهان (k، 2) و(3، −6) متعامدان. ما قيمة k؟","QuestionTextEn":"Vectors (k, 2) and (3, −6) are perpendicular. What is k?","DetailedSolutionAr":"قانون التعامد بين متجهين: يكون حاصل الضرب النقطي صفراً. للمتجهين (k، 2) و(3، −6) نحسب (k،2) · (3،−6) = 3k + 2 × (−6) = 3k − 12. نساوي الناتج بالصفر: 3k − 12 = 0، إذن 3k = 12 ومنها k = 4. التحقق: 3 × 4 − 12 = 0.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Orthogonality rule: Two vectors are perpendicular exactly when their dot product is zero. For (k,2) and (3,−6), compute 3k + 2(−6) = 3k − 12. Solve 3k − 12 = 0 to obtain k = 4. Check: 3 × 4 − 12 = 0.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2577,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"-4","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2578,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2579,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"4","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2580,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"6","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل شرط التعامد.","En":"Use the orthogonality condition."},{"Ar":"اكتب الضرب القياسي بدلالة k وساوِه بالصفر.","En":"Express the dot product in k and set it to zero."}],"Title":{"Ar":"استنتاج مركبة مجهولة من شرط التعامد","En":"Find an unknown vector component from orthogonality"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"−4 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً −24.","En":"−4 gives dot product −24."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"-4"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"2 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً −6.","En":"2 gives dot product −6."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"2"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"4"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"6 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً 6.","En":"6 gives dot product 6."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"6"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"المتجهان (k، 2) و(3، −6) متعامدان. ما قيمة k؟","En":"Vectors (k, 2) and (3, −6) are perpendicular. What is k?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"التعامد يقتضي انعدام الضرب القياسي.","En":"Perpendicular vectors have zero dot product."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المتجهان غير صفريين؛ التعامد يفرض $3k+2(-6)=0$.","En":"Both vectors are nonzero; orthogonality requires $3k+2(-6)=0$."},{"Ar":"$3k=12$ ومنه $k=4$.","En":"$3k=12$, hence $k=4$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$4$","En":"$4$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"انتبه لإشارة المركبة السالبة.","En":"Preserve the negative component."},"FormulaLatex":"u\\perp v\\Rightarrow u\\cdot v=0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$3k-12=0\\Rightarrow k=4$","En":"$3k-12=0\\Rightarrow k=4$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$3(4)+2(-6)=0$","En":"$3(4)+2(-6)=0$"}},"TrackIds":[14,20],"CategoryId":14,"PrimarySkillId":63,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"استعمل شرط التعامد.","En":"Use the orthogonality condition."},{"Ar":"اكتب الضرب القياسي بدلالة k وساوِه بالصفر.","En":"Express the dot product in k and set it to zero."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"التعامد يقتضي انعدام الضرب القياسي.","En":"Perpendicular vectors have zero dot product."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المتجهان غير صفريين؛ التعامد يفرض $3k+2(-6)=0$.","En":"Both vectors are nonzero; orthogonality requires $3k+2(-6)=0$."},{"Ar":"$3k=12$ ومنه $k=4$.","En":"$3k=12$, hence $k=4$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$4$","En":"$4$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"انتبه لإشارة المركبة السالبة.","En":"Preserve the negative component."},"FormulaLatex":"u\\perp v\\Rightarrow u\\cdot v=0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$3k-12=0\\Rightarrow k=4$","En":"$3k-12=0\\Rightarrow k=4$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$3(4)+2(-6)=0$","En":"$3(4)+2(-6)=0$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"−4 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً −24.","En":"−4 gives dot product −24."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً −6.","En":"2 gives dot product −6."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"6 يعطي ضرباً نقطياً 6.","En":"6 gives dot product 6."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$التعامد يقتضي انعدام الضرب القياسي.

$u\perp v\Rightarrow u\cdot v=0$

1. المتجهان غير صفريين؛ التعامد يفرض $3k+2(-6)=0$.

2. $3k=12$ ومنه $k=4$.

$3k-12=0\Rightarrow k=4$

$4$ بلا وحدة قياس

$3(4)+2(-6)=0$

انتبه لإشارة المركبة السالبة.$mw$,$mw$Perpendicular vectors have zero dot product.

$u\perp v\Rightarrow u\cdot v=0$

1. Both vectors are nonzero; orthogonality requires $3k+2(-6)=0$.

2. $3k=12$, hence $k=4$.

$3k-12=0\Rightarrow k=4$

$4$ Dimensionless

$3(4)+2(-6)=0$

Preserve the negative component.$mw$),
(696,648,$mw$5E86F3D9D36E093F8D71DAD7BEA67A3B9AA9556070A481BB913CD2C993B827EF$mw$,$mw$fed471008aa5f95a55d5aa3fd0e39310$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":648,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":14,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"حساب جيب تمام الزاوية بين متجهين من الضرب النقطي","TitleEn":"Find cosine of angle between two vectors","QuestionTextAr":"ما قيمة cos(θ) بين المتجهين (1، 0) و(1، √3)؟","QuestionTextEn":"What is cos θ between vectors (1, 0) and (1, √3)?","DetailedSolutionAr":"الضرب النقطي 1، والطولان 1 و2، لذا cos(θ) = 1 ÷ (1 × 2) = 1/2.","DetailedSolutionEn":"The dot product is 1, and the magnitudes are 1 and 2. Thus cos θ = 1/(1 × 2) = 1/2.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2581,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"\\frac12","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2582,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2583,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2584,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"تحتاج إلى الضرب النقطي وطولي المتجهين.","En":"You need the dot product and both vector norms."},{"Ar":"اقسم الضرب النقطي على حاصل ضرب الطولين.","En":"Divide the dot product by the product of the two norms."}],"Title":{"Ar":"حساب جيب تمام الزاوية بين متجهين من الضرب النقطي","En":"Find cosine of angle between two vectors"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"\\frac12"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"√3/2 هو جيب الزاوية هنا، لا جيب تمامها.","En":"√3/2 is the sine here, not the cosine."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\frac{\\sqrt3}{2}"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"1 يعني أن المتجهين في الاتجاه نفسه، وهذا غير صحيح.","En":"1 would mean the vectors have the same direction, which they do not."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"2 أكبر من 1 فلا يكون جيب تمام زاوية حقيقية.","En":"2 exceeds 1 and cannot be a real angle cosine."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"2"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"ما قيمة cos(θ) بين المتجهين (1، 0) و(1، √3)؟","En":"What is cos θ between vectors (1, 0) and (1, √3)?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون جيب تمام الزاوية بين متجهين غير صفريين: $\\cos\\theta=(u\\cdot v)/(\\|u\\|\\|v\\|)$.","En":"Angle formula for nonzero vectors: $\\cos\\theta=(u\\cdot v)/(\\|u\\|\\|v\\|)$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الضرب النقطي $1(1)+0(\\sqrt3)=1$، وطولا المتجهين 1 و$\\sqrt{1+3}=2$.","En":"Dot product is $1(1)+0(\\sqrt3)=1$, and the norms are 1 and $\\sqrt{1+3}=2$."},{"Ar":"بما أن الطولين غير صفريين، $\\cos\\theta=1/(1\\cdot2)=1/2$.","En":"Both norms are nonzero, so $\\cos\\theta=1/(1\\cdot2)=1/2$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1/2$","En":"$1/2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستخدم مركبة واحدة بدلاً من طول المتجه.","En":"Do not replace a norm with one component."},"FormulaLatex":"\\cos\\theta=\\frac{u\\cdot v}{\\|u\\|\\|v\\|}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1/(1\\times\\sqrt{1+3})$","En":"$1/(1\\times\\sqrt{1+3})$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"طول المتجه الثاني 2 والضرب النقطي 1.","En":"The second norm is 2 and the dot product is 1."}},"TrackIds":[14,20],"CategoryId":14,"PrimarySkillId":63,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"تحتاج إلى الضرب النقطي وطولي المتجهين.","En":"You need the dot product and both vector norms."},{"Ar":"اقسم الضرب النقطي على حاصل ضرب الطولين.","En":"Divide the dot product by the product of the two norms."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون جيب تمام الزاوية بين متجهين غير صفريين: $\\cos\\theta=(u\\cdot v)/(\\|u\\|\\|v\\|)$.","En":"Angle formula for nonzero vectors: $\\cos\\theta=(u\\cdot v)/(\\|u\\|\\|v\\|)$."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"الضرب النقطي $1(1)+0(\\sqrt3)=1$، وطولا المتجهين 1 و$\\sqrt{1+3}=2$.","En":"Dot product is $1(1)+0(\\sqrt3)=1$, and the norms are 1 and $\\sqrt{1+3}=2$."},{"Ar":"بما أن الطولين غير صفريين، $\\cos\\theta=1/(1\\cdot2)=1/2$.","En":"Both norms are nonzero, so $\\cos\\theta=1/(1\\cdot2)=1/2$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1/2$","En":"$1/2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تستخدم مركبة واحدة بدلاً من طول المتجه.","En":"Do not replace a norm with one component."},"FormulaLatex":"\\cos\\theta=\\frac{u\\cdot v}{\\|u\\|\\|v\\|}","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1/(1\\times\\sqrt{1+3})$","En":"$1/(1\\times\\sqrt{1+3})$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"طول المتجه الثاني 2 والضرب النقطي 1.","En":"The second norm is 2 and the dot product is 1."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"√3/2 هو جيب الزاوية هنا، لا جيب تمامها.","En":"√3/2 is the sine here, not the cosine."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 يعني أن المتجهين في الاتجاه نفسه، وهذا غير صحيح.","En":"1 would mean the vectors have the same direction, which they do not."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"2 أكبر من 1 فلا يكون جيب تمام زاوية حقيقية.","En":"2 exceeds 1 and cannot be a real angle cosine."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$قانون جيب تمام الزاوية بين متجهين غير صفريين: $\cos\theta=(u\cdot v)/(\|u\|\|v\|)$.

$\cos\theta=\frac{u\cdot v}{\|u\|\|v\|}$

1. الضرب النقطي $1(1)+0(\sqrt3)=1$، وطولا المتجهين 1 و$\sqrt{1+3}=2$.

2. بما أن الطولين غير صفريين، $\cos\theta=1/(1\cdot2)=1/2$.

$1/(1\times\sqrt{1+3})$

$1/2$ بلا وحدة قياس

طول المتجه الثاني 2 والضرب النقطي 1.

لا تستخدم مركبة واحدة بدلاً من طول المتجه.$mw$,$mw$Angle formula for nonzero vectors: $\cos\theta=(u\cdot v)/(\|u\|\|v\|)$.

$\cos\theta=\frac{u\cdot v}{\|u\|\|v\|}$

1. Dot product is $1(1)+0(\sqrt3)=1$, and the norms are 1 and $\sqrt{1+3}=2$.

2. Both norms are nonzero, so $\cos\theta=1/(1\cdot2)=1/2$.

$1/(1\times\sqrt{1+3})$

$1/2$ Dimensionless

The second norm is 2 and the dot product is 1.

Do not replace a norm with one component.$mw$),
(697,650,$mw$84F9BFC2642E1332866FFD31403C617FA107B59C27B964C9F4B4F2D6D4D11D4D$mw$,$mw$5cdf2191f459a3d63a3b0c77d6edace0$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":650,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":14,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"إيجاد بُعد الفضاء المولّد من متجهين مستقلين","TitleEn":"Find the dimension of a span of independent vectors","QuestionTextAr":"ما بُعد الفضاء المولّد بالمتجهين (1، 0، 1) و(0، 1، 1) في R³؟","QuestionTextEn":"What is the dimension of the span of (1, 0, 1) and (0, 1, 1) in R³?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المتجهان غير متناسبين، ولا يمكن كتابة أحدهما كمضاعف للآخر؛ إذن مستقلان وبُعد فضائهما المولّد 2.","DetailedSolutionEn":"Neither vector is a scalar multiple of the other, so they are independent and their span has dimension 2.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2589,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2590,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2591,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2592,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"3","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"اختبر علاقة خطية صفرية.","En":"Test a zero linear combination."},{"Ar":"قارن المركبات لإيجاد معاملات التركيب الصفري.","En":"Compare components to determine coefficients of a zero combination."}],"Title":{"Ar":"إيجاد بُعد الفضاء المولّد من متجهين مستقلين","En":"Find the dimension of a span of independent vectors"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"0 يتطلب أن يكون الفضاء صفرياً، والمتجهان غير صفريين.","En":"0 would require a zero subspace, but the vectors are nonzero."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"0"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"1 يتطلب تبعية المتجهين، وهما مستقلان.","En":"1 requires dependence, but the vectors are independent."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"2"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"متجهان لا يستطيعان توليد فضاء بعده 3.","En":"Two vectors cannot span a three-dimensional space."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"3"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"ما بُعد الفضاء المولّد بالمتجهين (1، 0، 1) و(0، 1، 1) في R³؟","En":"What is the dimension of the span of (1, 0, 1) and (0, 1, 1) in R³?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتجهان مستقلان لأن المركبتين الأولى والثانية تفرضان انعدام معاملي التركيب الصفري.","En":"The vectors are independent because their first two coordinates force both coefficients in a zero combination to vanish."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نفترض $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$.","En":"Suppose $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$."},{"Ar":"المركبتان الأولى والثانية تفرضان $c_1=c_2=0$؛ إذن المتجهان مستقلان ويولدان فضاء بعده 2.","En":"The first two coordinates force $c_1=c_2=0$; the vectors are independent and span a space of dimension 2."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$2$","En":"$2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تساو بعد الفضاء المحيط بعد الفضاء المولد.","En":"Do not equate ambient dimension with span dimension."},"FormulaLatex":"\\dim\\operatorname{span}(v_1,v_2)=\\operatorname{rank}[v_1\\ v_2]","Substitution":{"Ar":"$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\\Rightarrow a=b=0$","En":"$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\\Rightarrow a=b=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}=1$","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}=1$"}},"TrackIds":[14,20],"CategoryId":14,"PrimarySkillId":62,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"اختبر علاقة خطية صفرية.","En":"Test a zero linear combination."},{"Ar":"قارن المركبات لإيجاد معاملات التركيب الصفري.","En":"Compare components to determine coefficients of a zero combination."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"المتجهان مستقلان لأن المركبتين الأولى والثانية تفرضان انعدام معاملي التركيب الصفري.","En":"The vectors are independent because their first two coordinates force both coefficients in a zero combination to vanish."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"نفترض $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$.","En":"Suppose $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$."},{"Ar":"المركبتان الأولى والثانية تفرضان $c_1=c_2=0$؛ إذن المتجهان مستقلان ويولدان فضاء بعده 2.","En":"The first two coordinates force $c_1=c_2=0$; the vectors are independent and span a space of dimension 2."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$2$","En":"$2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تساو بعد الفضاء المحيط بعد الفضاء المولد.","En":"Do not equate ambient dimension with span dimension."},"FormulaLatex":"\\dim\\operatorname{span}(v_1,v_2)=\\operatorname{rank}[v_1\\ v_2]","Substitution":{"Ar":"$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\\Rightarrow a=b=0$","En":"$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\\Rightarrow a=b=0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}=1$","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\0&1\\end{pmatrix}=1$"}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"0 يتطلب أن يكون الفضاء صفرياً، والمتجهان غير صفريين.","En":"0 would require a zero subspace, but the vectors are nonzero."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 يتطلب تبعية المتجهين، وهما مستقلان.","En":"1 requires dependence, but the vectors are independent."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"متجهان لا يستطيعان توليد فضاء بعده 3.","En":"Two vectors cannot span a three-dimensional space."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$المتجهان مستقلان لأن المركبتين الأولى والثانية تفرضان انعدام معاملي التركيب الصفري.

$\dim\operatorname{span}(v_1,v_2)=\operatorname{rank}[v_1\ v_2]$

1. نفترض $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$.

2. المركبتان الأولى والثانية تفرضان $c_1=c_2=0$؛ إذن المتجهان مستقلان ويولدان فضاء بعده 2.

$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\Rightarrow a=b=0$

$2$ بلا وحدة قياس

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}=1$

لا تساو بعد الفضاء المحيط بعد الفضاء المولد.$mw$,$mw$The vectors are independent because their first two coordinates force both coefficients in a zero combination to vanish.

$\dim\operatorname{span}(v_1,v_2)=\operatorname{rank}[v_1\ v_2]$

1. Suppose $c_1(1,0,1)+c_2(0,1,1)=0$.

2. The first two coordinates force $c_1=c_2=0$; the vectors are independent and span a space of dimension 2.

$a(1,0,1)+b(0,1,1)=(a,b,a+b)=0\Rightarrow a=b=0$

$2$ Dimensionless

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\0&1\end{pmatrix}=1$

Do not equate ambient dimension with span dimension.$mw$),
