(699,652,$mw$5075337AD78ACF04E6E151223E30863842B293B2E8E844C1F488A27D9A936939$mw$,$mw$c9863d636433f75238b153134e013b11$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":652,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":14,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"تحديد أكبر عدد من المتجهات المستقلة في مستوٍ","TitleEn":"Determine maximal independence within R²","QuestionTextAr":"في R² لدينا المتجهات (1، 2) و(3، 6) و(0، 1). ما أكبر عدد يمكن اختياره منها بحيث تكون مستقلة خطياً؟","QuestionTextEn":"In R² consider (1, 2), (3, 6), and (0, 1). What is the largest number of linearly independent vectors among them?","DetailedSolutionAr":"المتجه الثاني ثلاثة أضعاف الأول، أما الأول والثالث فمستقلان؛ لذلك العدد الأكبر 2، ولا يمكن وجود ثلاثة متجهات مستقلة في R².","DetailedSolutionEn":"The second vector is three times the first. The first and third are independent, so the maximum number is 2; three vectors cannot be independent in R².","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2597,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2598,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2599,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2600,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"3","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن متجهين غير متناسبين.","En":"Look for two nonproportional vectors."},{"Ar":"اختبر محدد زوج مناسب ثم استخدم بعد المستوى كحد أعلى.","En":"Test the determinant of a suitable pair and use the plane dimension as an upper bound."}],"Title":{"Ar":"تحديد أكبر عدد من المتجهات المستقلة في مستوٍ","En":"Determine maximal independence within R²"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"0 يتجاهل وجود متجه غير صفري.","En":"0 ignores the existence of a nonzero vector."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"0"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"1 أقل من حجم المجموعة المستقلة المبينة.","En":"1 is below the demonstrated independent set size."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"2"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"3 يتجاوز بُعد المستوى.","En":"3 exceeds the dimension of the plane."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"3"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"في R² لدينا المتجهات (1، 2) و(3، 6) و(0، 1). ما أكبر عدد يمكن اختياره منها بحيث تكون مستقلة خطياً؟","En":"In R² consider (1, 2), (3, 6), and (0, 1). What is the largest number of linearly independent vectors among them?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البعد الأعلى في المستوى اثنان؛ المتجهان الأول والثالث مستقلان.","En":"The plane has dimension two; the first and third vectors are independent."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المتجه الثاني ثلاثة أمثال الأول، فلا يمكن اختيار الثلاثة مستقلة.","En":"The second vector is three times the first, so all three cannot be independent."},{"Ar":"المتجهان $(1,2)$ و$(0,1)$ مستقلان لأن محدد عموديهما 1؛ وبُعد المستوى 2، إذن الحد الأقصى 2.","En":"Vectors $(1,2)$ and $(0,1)$ are independent because their column determinant is 1; the plane has dimension 2, so the maximum is 2."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$2$","En":"$2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"وجود ثلاثة متجهات لا يعني استقلالها جميعاً.","En":"Three vectors need not be independent."},"FormulaLatex":"\\operatorname{rank}[v_1\\ v_2\\ v_3]\\le2","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$، وهذا يثبت استقلال متجهين.","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$, proving two vectors are independent."}},"TrackIds":[14,20],"CategoryId":14,"PrimarySkillId":62,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"ابحث عن متجهين غير متناسبين.","En":"Look for two nonproportional vectors."},{"Ar":"اختبر محدد زوج مناسب ثم استخدم بعد المستوى كحد أعلى.","En":"Test the determinant of a suitable pair and use the plane dimension as an upper bound."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"البعد الأعلى في المستوى اثنان؛ المتجهان الأول والثالث مستقلان.","En":"The plane has dimension two; the first and third vectors are independent."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"المتجه الثاني ثلاثة أمثال الأول، فلا يمكن اختيار الثلاثة مستقلة.","En":"The second vector is three times the first, so all three cannot be independent."},{"Ar":"المتجهان $(1,2)$ و$(0,1)$ مستقلان لأن محدد عموديهما 1؛ وبُعد المستوى 2، إذن الحد الأقصى 2.","En":"Vectors $(1,2)$ and $(0,1)$ are independent because their column determinant is 1; the plane has dimension 2, so the maximum is 2."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$2$","En":"$2$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"وجود ثلاثة متجهات لا يعني استقلالها جميعاً.","En":"Three vectors need not be independent."},"FormulaLatex":"\\operatorname{rank}[v_1\\ v_2\\ v_3]\\le2","Substitution":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$، وهذا يثبت استقلال متجهين.","En":"$\\det\\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\\\2&1\\end{pmatrix}=1\\ne0$, proving two vectors are independent."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"0 يتجاهل وجود متجه غير صفري.","En":"0 ignores the existence of a nonzero vector."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"1 أقل من حجم المجموعة المستقلة المبينة.","En":"1 is below the demonstrated independent set size."},"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"3 يتجاوز بُعد المستوى.","En":"3 exceeds the dimension of the plane."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$البعد الأعلى في المستوى اثنان؛ المتجهان الأول والثالث مستقلان.

$\operatorname{rank}[v_1\ v_2\ v_3]\le2$

1. المتجه الثاني ثلاثة أمثال الأول، فلا يمكن اختيار الثلاثة مستقلة.

2. المتجهان $(1,2)$ و$(0,1)$ مستقلان لأن محدد عموديهما 1؛ وبُعد المستوى 2، إذن الحد الأقصى 2.

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\2&1\end{pmatrix}=1\ne0$

$2$ بلا وحدة قياس

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\2&1\end{pmatrix}=1\ne0$، وهذا يثبت استقلال متجهين.

وجود ثلاثة متجهات لا يعني استقلالها جميعاً.$mw$,$mw$The plane has dimension two; the first and third vectors are independent.

$\operatorname{rank}[v_1\ v_2\ v_3]\le2$

1. The second vector is three times the first, so all three cannot be independent.

2. Vectors $(1,2)$ and $(0,1)$ are independent because their column determinant is 1; the plane has dimension 2, so the maximum is 2.

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\2&1\end{pmatrix}=1\ne0$

$2$ Dimensionless

$\det\begin{pmatrix}1&0\\2&1\end{pmatrix}=1\ne0$, proving two vectors are independent.

Three vectors need not be independent.$mw$),
(700,653,$mw$1E505E2E5BDB755A12DE93EBE970B3E77322410244236775AF188375A7E2BC27$mw$,$mw$50f682ec6b5fae68dc20576771798022$mw$,$mw$$mw$,$mw${"Id":653,"StageId":4,"CategoryId":36,"Points":10,"TitleAr":"استنتاج نهاية متتالية متزايدة ومحدودة","TitleEn":"Find a bounded increasing sequence's limit","QuestionTextAr":"متتالية aₙ = 1 − 1/n للأعداد الطبيعية n ≥ 1. ما نهايتها؟","QuestionTextEn":"For n ≥ 1, aₙ = 1 − 1/n. What is its limit?","DetailedSolutionAr":"كلما كبر n صغر 1/n نحو الصفر، وتزداد aₙ نحو 1 من الأسفل. لذا نهايتها 1.","DetailedSolutionEn":"As n increases, 1/n decreases to zero. Thus aₙ increases toward 1 from below.","YoutubeSolutionUrl":null,"EditorialDetailsJson":null,"Options":[{"Id":2601,"Order":1,"LatexCode":"0","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2602,"Order":2,"LatexCode":"1","IsCorrect":true},{"Id":2603,"Order":3,"LatexCode":"2","IsCorrect":false},{"Id":2604,"Order":4,"LatexCode":"\\infty","IsCorrect":false}]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"Hints":[{"Ar":"افصل الحد الثابت عن الحد الذي يتغير مع العدد الطبيعي.","En":"Separate the constant from the term that varies with the natural number."},{"Ar":"استخدم نهاية مقلوب العدد الطبيعي عند اللانهاية ثم قانون نهاية الفرق.","En":"Use the reciprocal's limit at infinity, then the difference rule."}],"Title":{"Ar":"استنتاج نهاية متتالية متزايدة ومحدودة","En":"Find a bounded increasing sequence's limit"},"Points":10,"Options":[{"Reason":{"Ar":"0 قيمة الحد الأول، لا النهاية.","En":"0 is the first term, not the limit."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"0"},{"Reason":null,"ErrorType":"","IsCorrect":true,"LatexCode":"1"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"جميع الحدود أصغر من 1 فلا تقترب من 2.","En":"All terms are below 1, so they cannot approach 2."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"2"},{"Reason":{"Ar":"المتتالية محصورة بين صفر وواحد.","En":"The sequence is bounded between zero and one."},"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","IsCorrect":false,"LatexCode":"\\infty"}],"StageId":4,"Question":{"Ar":"متتالية aₙ = 1 − 1/n للأعداد الطبيعية n ≥ 1. ما نهايتها؟","En":"For n ≥ 1, aₙ = 1 − 1/n. What is its limit?"},"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون نهاية الفرق: $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1/n)$، و$1/n\\to0$.","En":"Difference limit rule: $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1/n)$; the reciprocal tends to zero."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"عندما $n\\to\\infty$ فإن $1/n\\to0$.","En":"As $n\\to\\infty$, $1/n\\to0$."},{"Ar":"بقانون فرق النهايات $\\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$.","En":"By the difference limit law, $\\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1$","En":"$1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط نهاية المقلوب بنهاية المتتالية كلها.","En":"Do not confuse the reciprocal's limit with the entire sequence's limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}1/n$","En":"$1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}1/n$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$|a_n-1|=1/n$؛ لأي $\\varepsilon>0$ يكفي اختيار $n>1/\\varepsilon$.","En":"$|a_n-1|=1/n$; for any $\\varepsilon>0$, choose $n>1/\\varepsilon$."}},"TrackIds":[13,20],"CategoryId":36,"PrimarySkillId":74,"DifficultyLevel":1,"SecondarySkillIds":[]}$mw$::jsonb,$mw${"DifficultyLevel":1,"Hints":[{"Ar":"افصل الحد الثابت عن الحد الذي يتغير مع العدد الطبيعي.","En":"Separate the constant from the term that varies with the natural number."},{"Ar":"استخدم نهاية مقلوب العدد الطبيعي عند اللانهاية ثم قانون نهاية الفرق.","En":"Use the reciprocal's limit at infinity, then the difference rule."}],"Solution":{"Idea":{"Ar":"قانون نهاية الفرق: $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1/n)$، و$1/n\\to0$.","En":"Difference limit rule: $\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1/n)$; the reciprocal tends to zero."},"Unit":{"Ar":"بلا وحدة قياس","En":"Dimensionless"},"Steps":[{"Ar":"عندما $n\\to\\infty$ فإن $1/n\\to0$.","En":"As $n\\to\\infty$, $1/n\\to0$."},{"Ar":"بقانون فرق النهايات $\\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$.","En":"By the difference limit law, $\\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$."}],"Result":{"Ar":"$1$","En":"$1$"},"CommonError":{"Ar":"لا تخلط نهاية المقلوب بنهاية المتتالية كلها.","En":"Do not confuse the reciprocal's limit with the entire sequence's limit."},"FormulaLatex":"\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}(1-1/n)=1-0","Substitution":{"Ar":"$1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}1/n$","En":"$1-\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}1/n$"},"Verification":{"Ar":"$|a_n-1|=1/n$؛ لأي $\\varepsilon>0$ يكفي اختيار $n>1/\\varepsilon$.","En":"$|a_n-1|=1/n$; for any $\\varepsilon>0$, choose $n>1/\\varepsilon$."}},"Distractors":[{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"0 قيمة الحد الأول، لا النهاية.","En":"0 is the first term, not the limit."},"Order":1},{"ErrorType":"","Reason":null,"Order":2},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"جميع الحدود أصغر من 1 فلا تقترب من 2.","En":"All terms are below 1, so they cannot approach 2."},"Order":3},{"ErrorType":"incorrect-option","Reason":{"Ar":"المتتالية محصورة بين صفر وواحد.","En":"The sequence is bounded between zero and one."},"Order":4}]}$mw$,$mw$قانون نهاية الفرق: $\lim_{n\to\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\lim_{n\to\infty}(1/n)$، و$1/n\to0$.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}(1-1/n)=1-0$

1. عندما $n\to\infty$ فإن $1/n\to0$.

2. بقانون فرق النهايات $\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$.

$1-\lim_{n\to\infty}1/n$

$1$ بلا وحدة قياس

$|a_n-1|=1/n$؛ لأي $\varepsilon>0$ يكفي اختيار $n>1/\varepsilon$.

لا تخلط نهاية المقلوب بنهاية المتتالية كلها.$mw$,$mw$Difference limit rule: $\lim_{n\to\infty}(1-1/n)=1-\lim_{n\to\infty}(1/n)$; the reciprocal tends to zero.

$\lim_{n\to\infty}(1-1/n)=1-0$

1. As $n\to\infty$, $1/n\to0$.

2. By the difference limit law, $\lim(1-1/n)=1-0=1$.

$1-\lim_{n\to\infty}1/n$

$1$ Dimensionless

$|a_n-1|=1/n$; for any $\varepsilon>0$, choose $n>1/\varepsilon$.

Do not confuse the reciprocal's limit with the entire sequence's limit.$mw$);
